                <pb facs="0376" n="367" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg367"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859B.01/194c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Godthaab</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Penfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-27T21:00:00-04:00">May 27, 1940—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Our telegram No. 9, May 27, 5 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>You may say to Governor Svane that we have been informed by Minister de
                        Kauffmann that he not only approves of the transaction and believes its
                        conclusion to be in the best interest of Greenland, but is prepared to sign
                        the necessary documents and pay the purchase price of $10,000 from funds now
                        available to him, immediately upon receipt through you of the authorization
                        of the Greenland authorities.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Please tactfully attempt to expedite this matter as we wish to despatch
                        the <hi rendition="#italic">Campbell</hi> to Greenland waters as soon as
                        possible.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
